  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">VIV poultry Africa booth</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The third edition of Poultry Africa will take place from the 4th - 6th October 2022 in Kigali, Rwanda. With an expected 2,000 visitors, Poultry Africa will bring together top-level visitors and delegations from the Sub-Sahara Africa region.In these times of rising feed ingredient prices, the rising demand for proteins and quality feed, the subject alternative ingredients for animal feed is a very relevant and a more and more upcoming subject. The current alternative feed sector in Sub Sahara Africa is still small, with a small number of companies (mostly start-ups) pioneering. Because the sector is still underdeveloped, the Poultry Africa event seems to be the right place to increase awareness, create new partnerships among players in the alternative feed sector and beyond, and showcase the potential of these new solutions.This project enables important stakeholders in alternative feeds, among others black soldier fly (BSF), to join forces and present their futureproof feed solutions. The project entails:1.	Showcasing alternative feed solutions with a booth at Poultry Africa;2.	Organisation of a session on alternative feed ingredients at the Leadership Conference of Poultry Africa;3.	Organisation of a seminar on technical best practices;4.	Matchmaking between exhibitors and new potential business partners.</narrative>
  </description>
